OL,3,GNEWSARare WW1 howitzer trophy gun saved
OL,4,Afrom scrapyard
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of only two short-barrelled 10.5cm
OL,7,Fhowitzer trophy guns believed to have
OL,8,Fsurvived in the UK has been saved from
OL,9,Fthe scrapyard by a World War One
OL,10,Fmuseum.
OL,12,FThe German gun was given to St
OL,13,FBoswells, a village in the Scottish
OL,14,FBorders near Melrose, after the war.
OL,16,F"Local veteran George Oliver took
OL,17,Fexception to it and he and his
OL,18,Fex-service pals tipped it into the
OL,19,FRiver Tweed, ironically saving it from
OL,20,Fthe scrap man in the 1930s," said Taff
OL,21,FGillingham, from Great War Huts near
OL,22,FBury St Edmunds, Suffolk.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
